## Test result

`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → **4925 passed, 299 skipped,
5 deselected**. No failures.

Eval: 26 cases, `url_exact` 26/26, `auth_header_exact` 26/26, `payload_shape`
26/26, `no_secret_leak` 26/26, **aggregate 0.9000** vs a 0.90 threshold.
`live_smoke` still **not run** — scored zero, not skipped. The Databricks CLI
profile now authenticates, but the gateway reachable from this machine is
`/ai-gateway/anthropic`, an Anthropic-protocol proxy, not an OpenAI-shaped
`/chat/completions` endpoint, and no external provider key is configured.

End-to-end over real HTTP against a local OpenAI-compatible server, with every
`DATABRICKS_*` variable deleted: 6/6 — path not doubled, no `Authorization` when
keyless, model from the declared default, tools passed through, content extracted,
and `ValidationError` naming `ONTOBRICKS_LLM_BASE_URL` when only a workspace is
configured.

ruff: **F-rule (real-bug) findings identical to HEAD at 67**; total 4705 → 4699,
six fewer. The F-rule delta check earned its keep: it caught **8 `F821 undefined
name`** the mechanical rename left in `mapping.py` and `ontology.py` — code paths
the 4925 tests do not cover. Tests alone would have shipped those.

New guard: `TestLLMRequestFieldNames` asserts the JS request field and the route
that reads it agree — the P3d hazard, where one side of an HTTP boundary changes
and a one-sided test suite stays green. Verified by re-injecting the regression
(2 failures) and reverting.

